opic into a focused, reportable story."}, {"id": "805f6999-0a4b-43e4-915b-45ca5582f8a0", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reporting plans", "children": [{"id": "9cd3803b-55d6-4f0e-b4a7-3a04ea00142b", "type": "concept", "title": "Source lists"}, {"id": "96998cd5-1750-43cf-84c7-971ff9fbe233", "type": "concept", "title": "Document searches"}, {"id": "2403e62d-8846-441c-9149-25a3d5df5cfa", "type": "concept", "title": "Interview targets"}, {"id": "4b6aa01f-6418-4cc8-be0e-47ea968fe088", "type": "concept", "title": "Deadline planning"}], "description": "Reporting plans keep writers from drifting and help them gather the right evidence efficiently."}]}, {"id": "e475f985-9cc1-49ec-9c33-6edd029e84c4", "type": "topic", "title": "Leads, Nut Grafs, Story Structure, and the Inverted Pyramid", "description": "Practice concise openings and structures that help audiences quickly understand what matters and why.", "children": [{"id": "8d87898d-6a17-4aeb-8b2e-702f60cf45ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Leads", "children": [{"id": "d2c14e32-5615-43d4-b3a0-cef6899f9b12", "type": "concept", "title": "Summary leads"}, {"id": "f29a28f7-d96d-4009-811b-5fd97ec7a280", "type": "concept", "title": "Anecdotal leads"}, {"id": "8bae3cd9-2a37-4f9c-a8e9-39d8dc6017e3", "type": "concept", "title": "Delayed leads"}, {"id": "2cb38c85-b7a0-4362-81e4-566292d7c872", "type": "concept", "title": "Avoiding cliches"}], "description": "Leads teach economy: the writer must earn attention without distorting what happened."}, {"id": "f07a22ef-fcbb-4123-b868-d29ae80f1e1c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Nut grafs", "children": [{"id": "ec52ed84-8827-4d7f-8484-2a5140fdb3fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Story significance"}, {"id": "2df87a20-0043-49dc-8783-a3db47c95296", "type": "concept", "title": "Scope"}, {"id": "82b2536f-5893-4bb3-a39e-4e5e1d918d6a", "type": "concept", "title": "Central tension"}, {"id": "94658a33-6b94-44a9-9145-ea509bc722c2", "type": "concept", "title": "Reader payoff"}], "description": "The nut g